  The reel_script and caption say the three youths were brought to the station and that the police confiscated the cars, but the article says the cars were confiscated and the three youths were taken to the station, so this matches; however, the caption says 'வழக்குப்பதிவு செய்யாமல் போலீசார் திருந்த வாய்ப்பு அளித்தனர்' which is consistent with the article, so no issue there.
  The slides_spec line 'படித்தவர்களாக இருந்தும் தவறு செய்ததற்கு வருத்தம்' and the reel_script 'படித்தவராக இருந்தும் தவறு செய்ததற்கு அவமானமாக உள்ளதாக தெரிவித்தார்' mix the speaker's statement that he is an engineering graduate with the general claim about all three youths, which the article attributes only to one of them ('அவர்களில் ஒருவர்'), so the reel_script wrongly generalizes a single youth's remark to the group.
  The caption and reel_script state the incident happened on 'நவம்பர் 22ம் தேதி' with no year in the article; the caption's '2026' year is an invented detail not present in the article.
  The reel_script states that 'அவர்களில் ஒருவர்' said the silencer was changed per friends' wishes, and the slides_spec says 'படித்தவர்களாக' for all three, mixing one youth's engineering-graduate statement with the group; the article only says the three were 'பட்டதாரிகள்' in general, so this is partially supported, but the 'அவமானமாக' phrasing is a stretch from the article's 'படித்த படிப்புக்கே அவமானமாக கருதுகிறேன்' which is about the degree, not the act.
